    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **256 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to match the new specification.\n\n### Behaviour changes\n- **New identity key** \u2014 `identityKey` is now the lower-case SHA-256 hex digest of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (a 64-char hex string), replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` string.\n- **Duplicate detection (409)** \u2014 unchanged in mechanism: keys off the whole `identityKey`, still skips owners flagged `deleted`, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first (earlier in the POST pipeline). But because the key now hashes telephone+email+soundex(lastName), two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** produce different keys and are no longer a hard duplicate.\n- **Soft match (`possibleDuplicate`)** \u2014 now triggers when the `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` match (previously: exact `lastName` case-insensitive + postcode + different telephone). This is the look-alike household case that's now admitted-and-flagged rather than rejected.\n- **Household-duplicate 409 removed** \u2014 the computed `householdId` no longer feeds duplicate detection at all. `AssignOwnerHousehold` still runs, because `householdId` is still used for household-size and membership-level logic.\n\n### Files changed\n- **`Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 a correct American Soundex encoder (H/W transparent, vowels+Y act as separators), shared by the identity key and the soft match.\n- **`OwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 computes the SHA-256 hex key over telephone/email/soundex(lastName).\n- **`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 matches on soundex(lastName) + postcode with a differing identity key.\n- **`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 javadoc updated (no code change; the 409 rule already keyed off `OwnerIdentity.identityKey` and skipped deleted).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** and **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 comments/schema doc updated to describe the hashed single-key model and the new `identityKey` shape/example.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserting the `[0-9a-f]{64}` shape, and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` asserting the collision 409) both pass, along with the rest of the suite.",
